<Content title="Planning, not permission." description="BunkMeter explains attendance numbers. Your institution’s records and policies determine your actual status." path="/disclaimer" eyebrow="Disclaimer">
 <p class="updated">Updated 27 September 2026</p>
 <h2>A calculation is not an official record</h2><p>BunkMeter is an independent planning tool. It is not affiliated with a university, college or regulator and does not provide official attendance certification or determine exam eligibility.</p>
 <h2>What the calculations assume</h2><p>Inputs describe whole, equally weighted lectures. Attending adds one to both attended and held counts; missing adds one only to held. The target applies to those counts. If your institution weights labs, combines sessions or rounds percentages differently, use its official method.</p>
 <p>Remaining lectures must be upcoming lectures that will count toward attendance. A recovery result assumes you attend every class in the stated run. A missed class changes the plan. A best-possible term finish assumes you attend all remaining lectures.</p>
 <h2>Leave and condonation</h2><p>There is no universal condonation allowance built into this tool. Days are not lectures, and approved leave does not necessarily become a present mark. Confirm the rules and adjusted counts with your institution.</p>
 <h2>Use your judgment</h2><p>Check your official portal and course policy before making decisions. Results depend on the numbers entered and do not guarantee permission to miss classes. BunkMeter is provided as a planning aid, subject to the <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.</p>
 <h2>Commercial disclosures</h2><p>This release includes no advertising, paid features or affiliate referrals. Any future commercial relationships will be identified where relevant.</p>
 <p><a href="/contact">Report incorrect or misleading information.</a></p>
</Content>
